    "q-5902": {
      "dom_id": "step-q5902",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$\\frac{4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x+1}{x-5}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We can calculate $\\frac{4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x+1}{x-5}$ using synthetic division.\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process, we arrive at the following:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $4$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $20$ | $110$ | $545$ |\n|  | $4$ | $22$ | $109$ | $546$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x+1}{x-5}=4{x}^{2}+22x+109+\\frac{546}{x-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
